# CG Panel / Desk UI

Vocabulary and ownership: see `cg.mdc`.

**Panel layout (top to bottom, no left column):** (1) **Monitor bar** — one row, same in both modes: Back + `Package:` name + Studio/Direct + sync (`On air ×N`, fixed slot) | small Preview | **Take →** | small Program (no text labels, hover titles only). Direct keeps both monitors; Take is disabled once the package exists (Direct auto-saves; unsaved package shows **Create**). Package settings at the right, label above each control, in one row: Channel／Source, Appear (+ ms, room reserved), Look, monitor Alpha/Dim, Enlarge Program (`open_in_full`), **Copy OBS**, **Delete package** (`mat-flat-button.danger-btn`). Nothing in the bar changes position when mode / Fade-Cut switches. Below 1120px the settings hide behind a **Package 設定** button and open as a floating glass card (scrim click or Esc closes); monitors always stay. (2) **Layers strip**, always visible: one card per Layer (16:9 monitor in Package Look + name + On/Off `.cg-switch`, drag to reorder, horizontal `cdkDropList`), `…` on the card only opens that Layer's 設定 tab (`?tab=settings`, consumed once by `cg-layer-edit`); Layers Alpha/Dim and the catalog (`+ Logo`, `+ Clock`…) on the right. Click the selected card again to close the desk. (3) **Layer panel** (router outlet). Package level owns only Copy OBS + Delete package; Layer level owns Copy to package + Copy layer OBS + Delete layer (設定 tab) — never two homes. Host is a size container; breakpoint 1120px (`@container`): below it the bar stacks and a 收起 monitor button appears (960 screen).

## Edit mode (per package, localStorage `cg-package-edit-mode:{id}`)
| Mode | Monitors | Package mix | Take |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Studio mode** ON (default) | Pending \| On air on Package column | Waits for **Take**: name, role, Appear, Package Look, Layer existence / On-Off / z-order | Required |
| **Studio mode** OFF (= Direct) | One On air monitor | Auto-saves (debounced ~450ms) + Realtime broadcast | Hidden once package exists (first **Create** still needed); turning Studio off while dirty promotes immediately |

Layer content is never gated by Package Take (see Ownership in `cg.mdc`). Hide-mid-edit workflow: Package Off → Take → edit Layer → On → Take. Skipping Take after Off can still hit OBS while visible — accepted risk.

## Layer desk has no Studio mode
Layer content (Logo and Subtitle) is always Live: edits write through to DB, then publish to OBS (debounced ~450ms). When `CgService.onAirOutput` really lists the layer, the desk shows "This layer is on air. Edits go to OBS now." (reserved 28px row above the monitor).

## On air / Pending
- Studio: two 16:9 Stages — **Pending left** (`CgMixPreview`, draft), **On air right** (`CgOutputFrame`: the real `/o/<package token>` page in a 1920×1080 iframe, scaled). New unsaved Package: On air empty.
- Direct: one On air Stage (`CgOutputFrame`, not the draft). The same iframe instance stays mounted when switching Studio / Direct (no reload).
- **Enlarge On air** (`open_in_full`, header after Copy OBS) opens `CgOnAirDialog` (MatDialog, no animation): same `CgOutputFrame` at up to 1600px wide, with its own Alpha / Dim (shares `packageBackdrop`) and Close. Disabled until the package exists.
- Layer tiles use `CgMixPreview` (`wide`, `forceVisible`, Package pending Look) — same component as the desk monitor.
- Live cue (Up / Down / Blank / Paste / Load) and Cue Fade / Cut always update On air immediately in both modes. Alpha / Dim toggles sit next to **Package** and **Layers** — no Backdrop label.

## Controls & heights (Panel & Desk)
- `.cg-seg-btn`, `.cg-seg-toggle`, `.cg-pill`, `input`, `select`: uniform **28px** outer height, `box-sizing: border-box`.
- Inputs/selects: 1px border. `.cg-pill` is one recessed track (`--app-input-bg`, 1px `--app-button-border`, plus `--app-input-shadow`). Only the selected option is a button (`--app-button-primary-bg`); unselected options are text or icons with no fill, border, or shadow. Icon options sit in equal 24px cells so the glyphs share one center line. Multi-select text paint stays a merged button row.
- `.cg-seg-btn`: `height/min-height/max-height/line-height: 28px` (overrides Aero 32px).
- `.cg-monitor-toolbar` locked to 28px (`flex-shrink: 0; overflow: hidden`) so preview position is stable with or without Apply / Discard.

## Mouse wheel (every number input and dropdown)
Hover is enough (no focus needed); the field swallows the wheel. Directives `appCgWheel` (number `input`) and `appCgWheelSelect` (`select`) live in `core/domains/cg/cg-wheel.directive.ts`; they read the ngModel value and emit the next one (`appCgWheelChange`), the component writes the model the same way typing does. Up = increase; dropdown down = next option, stops at both ends. Alt = fine (step ÷10), Shift = coarse (×10; Windows moves the delta to `deltaX`). Off-grid values snap to the grid first (0.104 → 0.11). Clamped to `min` / `max`; an unchanged value emits nothing. Layer content is Live, so wheel edits go to OBS like typing (450ms debounce); no lock when on air.
- Steps: X / Y 0.1, Scale 0.05, ms 50 (fine 10, coarse 500; wheel floor `CG_WHEEL_MIN_FADE_MS` so it never turns into Cut), Size (% of Stage height) 0.1, 字距 0.01, 行距 0.05, Scale X / Y 0.05, Stroke 0.01, Shadow Angle 15 (fine 1, coarse 45, wraps 360 → 0), Shadow Distance / Radius 0.5, Gradient Angle 15 (same wrap as Shadow Angle). Breaking seconds 1 (fine 1, coarse 5, clamp 2–60), Breaking height 1 (fine 0.5, coarse 5). Ticker speed 0.5 (fine 0.1, coarse 5), gap 0.5 (fine 0.1, coarse 2), fade width 1. Ticker X / Y / Width / Height are stage pixels (step 1, fine 1, coarse 10; X −1920–1920, Y −1080–1080, width and height at least 8). Up hides Width. Title X / Y / Width 1 (design px on 1920; width clamp 8–1920; fine 0.1, coarse 10).
- Font wheel skips "Other…". Cue ms writes are debounced and coalesced in `CgService.patchLayerTransition` (draft updates at once).

## Always desktop (Panel only)
`/cg/new`, `/cg/edit/…` lock the phone viewport `width=1280`. The Panel itself has no `min-width`: it reflows on its own width with `@container` (≥1120px side by side; narrower stacks, big/small tabs wrap to two rows, monitors shrink, 收起 monitor buttons). **List** is responsive. Overlay `/o` and `/cg-live` stay `width=device-width`. Unlock when leaving Panel.

## Theme and buttons
- No fixed CG palette; follow the operator's Aero/Material + light/dark. Do not recreate `_cg-theme.scss`.
- Real Angular Material only, not hand-rolled `.cg-btn`:
  - Either-choice groups (Channel/Source, Fade/Cut, Color/B&W, Alpha/Dim, Live/Custom, Solid/Gradient, Cue Fade/Cut, Align, Anchor, Title tabs, Studio/Direct): `mat-button-toggle-group.cg-pill` (text groups also keep `cg-seg-toggle`). Anchor is the 3×3 `app-cg-anchor-grid` everywhere (stored values 1–9 unchanged); Layer / Title tabs use `.vb-tabs` instead of dropdowns.
  - One-shot actions (Delete / Copy OBS `content_copy` / Choose local image / catalog / cue / Copy): `mat-stroked-button.cg-seg-btn`.
  - Only **Create** / **Take** / Logo **Apply**: `mat-flat-button` primary.
  - Destructive: `mat-flat-button.danger-btn`.
  - **Studio / Direct** is a `.cg-pill` in the Package monitor toolbar only (labels Studio and Direct). Layer On/Off is `.cg-switch`.
  - Back is plain circular `<a class="cg-back">`. Package Copy OBS sits right after Package Alpha/Dim; Layers catalog is `margin-left: auto`.
- Sentence case labels; no uppercase transform.

## No global toolbar
`<app-toolbar>` hidden for Panel paths via `isCgPanelPath()`. **List** (`/cg`, `/cg/list`) uses the normal AppToolbar through `HeaderService` (title, back to Welcome, Refresh, New package). Panel keeps Back / Studio / Direct / Take inline.

## Layer desk
- Single preview for that one Layer, own local Alpha/Dim backdrop. Desk Look is **Layer Look only** (`layerLookOnly`); Package B&W does not grey the desk. Desk force-shows the layer even when Package Off (`forceVisible`). Desk does not bind Package Appear duration.
- Tiles: chrome on top (`drag_indicator` + z + On/Off), Stage thumb, **name** at bottom (custom `name`, or Element type if blank).
- **Every Layer desk (shared chrome in `_cg-desk-ui.scss`, mixin `desk-ui`)**: big VB.NET-style tabs **內容 | 樣式 | 設定** (Title: 內容 | 文字樣式 | 項目樣式 | 設定), one white panel, sections split by divider lines (no per-section boxes). Small tabs (Queue template, Title text slot, Item style template) are the same style one size smaller (30px). Long lists (Timezone, Clock Format Pattern) stay dropdowns; Fade／Cut, Align, B／I／U／S, Live／Custom stay pills.
  - **內容** order: green status bar ("● On air — 呢層出緊街，內容改動即時去 OBS，唔經 Take") → layer monitor (16:9, own content + own Look, ignores Package; 448px wide / 480px narrow with 收起 monitor) → 直播控制 → Queue／Cue list → 新增內容 last.
  - **樣式** order: ① Place (Anchor 3×3 `app-cg-anchor-grid` + X / Y / Width / Height, all px) → ② Style (shared `cg-text-style-editor`, font px) → ③ Layer 進出 (Fade／Cut + ms; Subtitle and Breaking only, labelled as the layer's own, not Package Appear; other layers show a note).
  - **設定**: Layer name, Layer Look, Copy to package (current package first, `Name (this package)` adds a draft copy), Layer OBS, Danger zone Delete layer (confirm).
  - Display only is px: font `px = vh × 10.8`; position / size `px = % × 19.2` (X, Width) / `% × 10.8` (Y, Height), px layouts ×1 (`cg-title-units.util.ts`); storage is unchanged and written only when the operator edits. Ticker speed / gap / fade width keep their own units. No Inherit / Follow package option.
- Greyscale is a per-layer host `filter` and always cuts. Package Appear only drives host opacity. Must not change z-order.

## Logo / Subtitle desk details
- Logo Anchor: 3×3 `app-cg-anchor-grid`. X / Y (px) / Scale inputs (no Unit / Width controls). X / Y labels say which edge they measure from (`From right`, `From top`); on a centered axis the input is a greyed `—` and the value is ignored (value kept in data). Desk **Outline** toggle (not saved, not OBS): thick yellow rim + red outer shadow.
- Subtitle desk: column A = monitor + Source + footer; column B = Cue (Up / Down / Blank / Fade-Cut, then ms) + filling queue; column C = Place (Anchor pill + **Align** left / center / right icon pill under it + X/Y/Scale (no Width); same ignored-axis `—` behaviour as Logo) then Style (no text-align control there). Empty Logo-only toolbar is hidden. Clock and Weather desk (right column): Background (optional image, Logo-style Source + Place + Outline + Clear), Text place (Anchor, Align, X / Y), Style (`cg-text-style-editor`), then Clock (format, language, timezone, Live/Custom, datetime + Push) or Weather (place search, unit mode). Background and text are placed separately. Title word Align is a Left / Center / Right pill.
- Cue bar icons: `keyboard_arrow_up` / `keyboard_arrow_down` / `content_paste`; **Blank** and **Load .txt / .srt** stay words.
- Title desk (`cg-title-desk`, full-width, replaces the left-monitor / right-config split for Title only): four big tabs **內容 / 文字樣式 / 項目樣式 / 設定** in VB.NET TabControl style (active tab white and joined to its panel, inactive grey and shorter; big 40px, small 30px; they wrap to two rows when narrow, never a dropdown). Each small-tab page is one panel, sections split by divider lines. **內容**: always-visible status bar (green when the layer is really on air), left = layer monitor (projected from `CgLayerEdit`, 16:9, 480px when narrow with a 收起 monitor button) + Live bar (On air switch, Headline / Subhead / Locator each with Push); right = Queue (drag, On/Off, `Template — text`, Edit, Delete, editing row highlighted + 正在編輯, Clear all) + eight template small tabs over one form (Push, or Update / Cancel). **文字樣式**: Primary / Secondary / Accent small tabs, mapping lines, other-slot summary, one shared `cg-text-style-editor` (`sizeUnit="px"`), read-only three-slot compare table. **項目樣式**: nine small tabs (Live last, independent copy of Story + locator, stated in the UI): Background, Background place (3×3 `app-cg-anchor-grid`, stored anchor values unchanged), per-word Text place (Anchor grid, From left / From bottom / Width in px, Align pill; heading names the text slot), Outline + Fade, read-only overview of all nine. **設定**: Layer name, Layer Look (this layer only, not Package Look), Copy to package, Copy layer OBS, Delete layer (confirm). Display is px: font `px = vh × 10.8`, Background place `px = % × 19.2` (X) / `% × 10.8` (Y); storage stays vh / % (`cg-title-units.util.ts`, written only when the operator edits). Title word slots were already stored as design px. Other layers keep their desks. Fade / Cut is the card transition, not Package Appear. On/Off and Live Push use the small Title broadcast, not a full snapshot. Editing queue text, Text style, or Item style still full-publishes.
- Breaking and Ticker desk share one queue (`cg-news-queue`): single line + insert position (top / after selected / bottom), textarea Append and Replace all, Load .txt (append, one line per row, blank lines ignored). List: drag handle, up/down, Enabled switch, edit, delete, Clear all (confirm). Breaking rejects a line over 24 characters and marks 20+ as small. While the layer is really on air, saving an edit offers **Apply now** (same id) or **Next pass** (new id). Left column: Background source. Right: queue | timing + background place + text place + Style. Breaking timing is seconds each, plus Fade/Cut. Ticker timing is Left / Up, speed, gap, fade on the exit and entry edges, and fade width. Text place is Anchor, X/Y, and Height (Breaking) or X / Y / Width / Height in stage pixels from the top left (Ticker, no Anchor). No Align control. Up draws one upright column. Letters and digits stay one cell each.
- Subtitle style: caption box is shrink-to-fit (Align moves it relative to the Anchor point; may overflow the Stage) and only wraps at Stage width. News = white fill, regular weight, `ScaleY` 1.11, `Spacing` 1.68. Black outline is a **behind** `-webkit-text-stroke` copy (fill on top); never stroke and fill on the same span (OBS CEF has no `paint-order`; 8-way `text-shadow` is jagged on CJK). Show is larger, slightly gold, thicker behind-stroke. Font dropdown: **Web fonts (any computer)** vs **Installed on OBS PC**; Other… is a text field for a local family name (`customFontOpen`). The chosen font paints the whole cue, including English and digits. Latin runs use 0.4× 字距 on a CJK face (so DFHei tracking does not loosen English); a Latin face (Oswald, Bebas Neue, Inter, Segoe UI, Roboto, Impact, Arial) uses the full 字距. CJK default: 華康中黑體 / JhengHei. Style row: Bold / Italic / Underline / Strikethrough (icons) and Solid / Gradient. Gradient adds End color + Angle (default 90°, left to right); Start is the existing Text Color. Decoration and gradient are fill-only so the stroke copy stays a single color and the line is not drawn twice. Gradient clip is the literal class `.sub-fill.is-gradient` (`-webkit-background-clip: text`); OBS CEF drops the keyword `text` when it is passed through a CSS variable and paints a solid bar. Absent paint fields keep the old look. Type size is Stage pixels (`--cg-uh` on the 1920×1080 canvas, see Stage canvas in `cg.mdc`), never `vh` / `cqh`; font-size stays on the inner text (`.ticker-text`, `.brk-text`), not the positioned box. `document.fonts.load` before cue swap (400ms cap).
